{"id":"mentoring-records","title":"Recording support and following through","minutes":3,"summary":"Keep useful adult records and respect their limits.","mediaIds":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Your outcome","html":"<p>Keep useful adult records and respect their limits.</p><p>Estimated reading time; check at your own pace. This is developmental support, separate from qualifications and formal assessment.</p>"},{"heading":"Four different records","html":"<p>A request describes a need and proposed arrangement. Linked visits preserve each occasion separately. An action records the next attempt; a follow-up records what happened or why it closed. Mentor assignment does not establish attendance. Lesson completion, delivered support and improved practice are separate things.</p>"},{"heading":"Who sees the notes","html":"<p>These are shared adult development records linked to your account, not anonymous notes. The coach, currently assigned mentor and authorised programme administrator can see them. Ask for a correction through the same record or coordinator; changes retain author/time and field-change metadata. Do not promise absolute confidentiality or use this as formal assessment.</p>"},{"heading":"Keep children out of the log","html":"<p>Do not enter children’s names, identifying details, health information, private family information, safeguarding allegations or identifiable child footage. Record adult behaviours and non-identifying observations only. Safeguarding concerns go immediately through the approved restricted reporting procedure, never the mentoring queue. See <a href=\"https://www.aysovolunteers.org/policy-safe-haven-cvpa/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AYSO Safe Haven</a> and <a href=\"https://www.ussoccer.com/safeguarding/report-a-concern\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">U.S. Soccer reporting guidance</a>; the local reporting procedure must be confirmed before pilot collection.</p>"},{"heading":"Follow through honestly","html":"<p>Use requested, arranging, confirmed, delivered, follow-up due, closed, postponed or cancelled. Confirmation needs the coach’s agreement and current mentor’s acceptance. Delivery requires a coach/mentor confirmation the visit happened. A past date is not attendance. Delivery must preserve outstanding follow-ups. Close only when actions have results or closure reasons. Retention and deletion, including backups, need an approved organisational policy; no fixed period is assumed.</p>"}],"quiz":[{"id":"mentoring-records-1","prompt":"A mentor is assigned and the proposed date is past. Was the visit delivered?","options":["Yes, automatically.","No; the coach or mentor must confirm attendance.","Only if the coach completed a quiz."],"correct":1,"explanation":"Assignment, elapsed time and lesson completion are not evidence of delivery."},{"id":"mentoring-records-2","prompt":"A draft note contains a child’s name and medical details. What next?","options":["Keep it because only staff can see it.","Copy it to the request topic.","Remove it from routine development notes and use the proper restricted process if required."],"correct":2,"explanation":"Mentoring records should describe adult practice without child-identifying information."},{"id":"mentoring-records-3","prompt":"A safeguarding disclosure arises. Where does it go?","options":["Immediately through the approved reporting procedure.","Into the next ordinary mentoring follow-up.","Into a public lesson reflection."],"correct":0,"explanation":"Do not delay reporting or put allegations in the mentoring queue."}],"takeaway":"Check one shared adult record for accuracy and agree the next follow-up.","sourceRefs":[]}
SCYS_JSON
, true, 512, JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR );
